              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "ladyT"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I used 12 oz of both artichoke hearts and peppers and extra mayo after discovering no sour cream in the fridge. I used garden veg cream cheese (again no 'plain' in the fridge) and added 3 cloves fresh roasted garlic. I also added too much garlic salt and threw in a cup or so of chopped romaine lettuce (I know, right!) to cut the saltiness. Turned out divinely and the lettuce added a nice crunch akin to chopped water chestnuts. Finally, I didn't use a crock pot but baked it on low at 250F in the serving dish since I am taking it to a garden party!",
            "datePublished": "2015-06-11T16:57:58.127Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Miss Hattie"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Excellent warm dip and very easy to make! I doubled the artichokes, like a lot of folks seem to do. I heated it in a covered glass dish in the oven (300 degrees for over an hour) rather than the crock pot and it turned out great! I also took a small amount of the red pepper and the tougher artichoke petals and pureed them in a mini food processor with the mayonnaise. It added some color and depth to the dish. Overall it was excellent and I will definitely make it again. Thanks for the recipe!",
            "datePublished": "2019-02-20T17:16:57.690Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
